
Analysis Description
--------------------
Examine whether or not a codon alignment is better fit by models which
permit multiple instantaneous substitutions. v0.2 adds a separate rate
for codon-island triple-hit rates

- __Requirements__: in-frame codon alignment and a phylogenetic tree

- __Citation__: Submitted; preprint at hyphy.org/resources/fmm.pdf

- __Written by__: Sergei L Kosakovsky Pond, Sadie Wisotsky and Alexander Lucaci

- __Contact Information__: spond@temple.edu

- __Analysis Version__: 1.0


>code => Universal
>Loaded a multiple sequence alignment with **17** sequences, **144** codons, and **1** partitions from `/Users/alex/Documents/selection-tutorial/data/21-empirical/bglobin.nex`
The number of omega rate classes to include in the model (permissible range = [1,10], default value = 3, integer): 
>rates => 3

>triple-islands => No


### Obtaining branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases under the nucleotide GTR model

>kill-zero-lengths => Yes
* Log(L) = -3925.80, AIC-c =  7930.03 (39 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  2.041

### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -3798.13, AIC-c =  7690.06 (46 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  2.234
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.3234

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -3657.89, AIC-c =  7420.00 (51 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.2773
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.027               |    32.612     |                                   |
|               0.995               |    58.741     |                                   |
|               4.703               |     8.647     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -3619.76, AIC-c =  7345.83 (52 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1683
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.7920
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.002               |    28.029     |                                   |
|               0.992               |    61.833     |                                   |
|               3.808               |    10.137     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -3619.74, AIC-c =  7347.88 (53 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1675
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.7874
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.0715
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.0715
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.006               |    28.484     |                                   |
|               1.000               |    61.336     |                                   |
|               3.781               |    10.181     |                                   |


